                "professional_network_id": "70304269",
                "title": "Founder & CEO",
                "description": "LOKKER (www.lokker.com) is a next-generation data privacy automation and forensic detection platform that protects companies and their customers from unauthorized online data collection and tracking. As Founder and CEO, I oversee the design and deployment of systems that operate at the deepest layers of internet architecture\u2014identifying and remediating privacy risks created by third-party tools such as pixels, cookies, tags, SDKs, and embedded JavaScript.\n\nOur technology continuously scans websites and network requests to detect unauthorized data flows and behavioral tracking, providing organizations with precise, real-time visibility into their data-sharing ecosystem. By combining automation, browser-level telemetry, and forensic analytics, Lokker enables companies to measure, document, and block noncompliant data transmissions before they occur.\n\nUnder my leadership, Lokker has evolved into a trusted privacy operations platform used by enterprises in regulated sectors including healthcare, finance, and insurance. The company\u2019s mission reflects a fundamental shift in privacy compliance\u2014from static policy checklists to dynamic, technical enforcement at the infrastructure level. Our work directly supports compliance with major regulatory frameworks such as the CCPA, CPRA, GDPR, and HIPAA, as well as emerging U.S. state privacy laws, while helping companies maintain operational efficiency and transparency.\n\nBy bridging the gap between legal privacy requirements and technical implementation, Lokker enables organizations to translate compliance obligations into measurable, enforceable controls across their digital ecosystem.",
